Z||000003||DrRodey||12-28-2000||03:56 PM||||Depending on what your gonna be doing with it determins what you want.  In general it should come up to the bottom of your chin.  Longer if you are gonna be doing more free riding/Carving Shorter if you are gonna be doing more freestyle but keep it between the top of your shoulders and the bottom of your nose.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||12-28-2000||06:00 PM||||ok. thanks. actually got one for pretty cheap and been wonderinr about it. guess i lucked out 'cause it's right in there.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||12-28-2000||11:46 PM||||Im 6'0", 165lbs, and I've got a 153cm board.  It came up to my chin when I bough it, but i have grown a bit since then.  I do a lot of freeride, and little freestyle, but having the shorter board gives me alot more agility in the gladed runs.  I love going through the trees!<P>Have fun with the boardin!||||reg||1
